{"episodes":{"196750":"As a body of low pressure moved over the Atlantic Ocean, shallow convection continued to survive offshore with showers lingering near the southeastern Florida coast during the morning of October 24th.","196779":"Showers brought gusty outflow winds to northern Utah.","196781":"Scattered storms developed along a cold front in northeast Kansas and gradually formed into a line. These storms produced many reports of 55-65 wind gusts and a few instances of small hail up to one inch.","197007":"A shortwave moved into Iowa from South Dakota and Nebraska. Convection developed in ahead of, and with the shortwave axis, enhancing later in the evening with the development of the low level jet. ECAPE exceeded 1000 J/kg with effective shear of 30-40+ kts to aid in severe storm development. Additionally, directional shear in the low levels supported rotating updrafts supportive of hail development. Storms across the area produces penny to quarter sized hail with one report up to the size of golf balls.","197147":"A short wave trough brushed over northern Nevada along the ID/NV border, producing precipitation and some gusty winds north of the I-80 corridor.","197463":"During the afternoon hours of October 24th, storms brought widespread damaging wind gusts and a few large hail reports to portions of Missouri.","197578":"A storm system moved east across the area and led to the development of widespread showers and thunderstorms during the afternoon and evening hours of October 24th. A few of these storms become severe, producing hail up to quarter size and damaging wind gusts. A lightning strike near Keosauqua caused a fire that destroyed a historic church."},"events":[{"begin":"2024-10-24T03:37Z","county":"Humboldt","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2024-10-24T04:37Z","endLat":41.4536,"endLon":-117.6219,"episode":197147,"id":1219596,"injuries":0,"lat":41.4536,"location":"12.23 SE Orovada","lon":-117.6219,"magnitude":50.0,"magnitu